<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves up to $1.86 bln March 14.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves up to $1.86 bln March 14.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday its net international reserves stood at $1.86 billion on March 14, up $12 million from the week before.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.83 billion at the end of last year, up $274 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
